## Why This Is Asked
This question probes designing a scalable, secure, multi-tenant pipeline that integrates Azure OpenAI with per-tenant governance, data redaction, and auditable logs. It emphasizes data flow clarity and practical constraints in production.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Event Hubs, Function/Stream Analytics pipelines
- Azure OpenAI with per-tenant prompts
- Cognitive Search KB grounding against Blob storage
- PII/PHI redaction with Text Analytics
- Data Lake per-tenant logs and auditability
- Azure AD RBAC and API Management canaries

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: tenant-scoped routing
async function routeTelemetry(event) {
  const tenant = extractTenant(event);
  const normalized = normalize(event);
  const prompt = buildPromptForTenant(tenant, normalized);
  const res = await openai.createChatCompletion({
    model: 'gpt-4o',
    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }],
  });
  await redactAndStore(tenant, event, res);
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency isolation per tenant at high ingestion rates?
- What strategies ensure prompt drift is detected and rolled back without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical APIM quota implementation and OpenAI routing for multi-tenant SaaS architectures.

## Key Concepts
- API Management policies with rate-limit-by-key
- Tenant-scoped routing via request headers
- Telemetry integration with Application Insights

## Code Example
```xml
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <set-variable name='TenantID' value='@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("x-tenant-id","default"))' />
    <rate-limit-by-key calls='60' renewal-period='60' key='@(context.Variables["TenantID"])' />
  </inbound>
</policies>
```

```javascript
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'] || 'default';
  const startTime = Date.now();

  try {
    const response = await callOpenAI(req.body);

    // Log usage to Application Insights
    context.log('TenantUsage', {
      tenantId,
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      duration: Date.now() - startTime,
      status: 'success'
    });

    return { status: 200, body: response };
  } catch (error) {
    context.log.error('TenantError', { tenantId, error: error.message });
    return { status: 500, body: { error: 'Service unavailable' } };
  }
};
```

## Validation Approach
Test with multiple tenant IDs using load testing tools, verify rate limits trigger at 60 requests/minute per tenant, and confirm telemetry appears in Application Insights queries.

